This is ClearPA, a medical SaaS application for prior authorization in ophthalmology.

CODE STANDARDS:
- TypeScript strict mode everywhere
- No any types — define proper interfaces
- All components in /components with barrel exports
- All API routes in /app/api
- All utility functions in /lib
- Custom hooks in /hooks

MEDICAL/HIPAA RULES:
- Never log patient data to console
- Never store PHI in localStorage or sessionStorage
- PDF text extraction happens client-side only
- All Supabase writes are coordinator-initiated, never automatic
- Error messages must never expose patient data

DESIGN RULES:
- Follow the design system in globals.css exactly
- All animations use CSS transitions or framer-motion — no abrupt state changes
- Every interactive element needs hover AND focus states
- Mobile-first responsive design
- Minimum touch target: 44px × 44px (Apple HIG standard)

AI INTEGRATION:
- Model: claude-sonnet-4-6 (from env var ANTHROPIC_MODEL)
- Always use streaming for analysis
- Never call Claude on the client — only via /app/api routes
- Parse [THINK] and [ANSWER] prefixes from Claude's streaming output

Do not deviate from these rules without explicit instruction.
